<v Justin Satinover>Come on.
<v Justin Satinover>快点。

00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:02.330
<v Lisa Satinover>Do it over.
<v Lisa Satinover>重来。

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:03.270
<v Young Darren Stein>No.
<v Young Darren Stein>不。

00:22:03.270 --> 00:22:15.880
<v Darren Stein>I should have said the weather and the camera stayed on me for my whole spiel. And then I would have announced either Lisa or Justin, and the camera would have gone to them. And Justin would do sports, and Lisa would do entertainment, like a real newscast.
<v Darren Stein>我应该说完天气，摄像机全程对着我。然后我会介绍丽莎或贾斯汀，摄像机才会切过去。贾斯汀会做体育，丽莎会做娱乐，像真正的新闻节目一样。

00:22:15.880 --> 00:22:26.740
<v Ira Glass>When you watch this as an adult, whose side are you on? Because I have to say, everybody else in the room is just trying to have fun, and there you are, baby Cecil B. DeMille.
<v Ira Glass>当你成年后看这段视频时，你站在哪一边？因为我得说，房间里其他每个人都在试图找乐子，而你却像个婴儿版的塞西尔·B·戴米尔。

00:22:26.740 --> 00:22:34.020
<v Darren Stein>I feel bad for my parents, more than anything. And the other kids. A little embarrassing too.
<v Darren Stein>比起其他任何事，我更替我的父母感到难过。还有其他孩子。也挺尴尬的。

00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:39.800
<v Ira Glass>So at some point, you actually get your hands on the movie camera, when you're 10 or 11. And you start filming all the time, right?
<v Ira Glass>所以到了某个阶段，你在 10 或 11 岁时真的拿到了摄像机。然后你开始一直拍，对吧？

00:22:39.800 --> 00:23:09.720
<v Darren Stein>Yeah, just filming stuff. When my parents would go out, we were trapped on this cul-de-sac in the hills of Encino. So we were sort of shipwrecked up there. And we had nothing else to do. It was sort of like, what do we do now? Let's make a movie. Mark Entous's backyard was this big, verdant, green lawn. And we'd go back there for the jungle films or for the adventure, Indiana Jones -type movies. Michael's house-- or in front of it, there was this canyon that was really dry. So we'd use that for the Vietnam movies.
<v Darren Stein>是的，只是随便拍拍。当我父母出门时，我们被困在恩西诺山丘这个死胡同里。所以我们有点像在那儿遇难了。我们没别的事可做。就好像，现在我们要干什么？让我们拍部电影吧。马克·恩图斯的后院有片大大的、青翠的草坪。我们会去那儿拍丛林电影，或者冒险电影，印第安纳·琼斯风格的。迈克尔家——或者在他家前面，有个非常干燥的峡谷。所以我们用那儿拍越南战争电影。

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:13.200
<v Male Child 1>Hold your breath, guys. It's a mine.
<v Male Child 1>屏住呼吸，伙计们。那是地雷。

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:15.150
<v Male Child 2>Oh, my God.
<v Male Child 2>噢，天哪。

00:23:15.150 --> 00:23:35.390
<v Ira Glass>They did a Holocaust film when he was 11. They did a film about the day after a nuclear war. In these early films, the high concepts were just excuses so that the main characters can run around and try to kill each other. There are a lot of gratuitous ninja moves. There's the prerequisite ketchup-as-gore. Because Darren was three years older than anybody on the street, it was easy for him to call the shots.
<v Ira Glass>他在 11 岁时拍过一部大屠杀电影。他们拍过一部关于核战后的电影。在这些早期影片中，崇高的理念只是为了让主角们可以跑来跑去并试图互相残杀。里面有很多无缘无故的忍者动作。有必不可少的番茄酱当作血浆。因为达伦比街上任何人都要大三岁，他发号施令很容易。

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:39.210
<v Adam Schell>Darren always seemed very powerful.
<v Adam Schell>达伦看起来总是很有权力。

00:23:39.210 --> 00:23:42.620
<v Ira Glass>This is Adam Schell, who lived on the cul-de-sac and appears in lots of the movies.
<v Ira Glass>这是亚当·谢尔，他住在死胡同里，在很多电影中都有出镜。

00:23:42.620 --> 00:23:49.500
<v Adam Schell>Darren was always the one that everybody looked up to. Basically, whatever Darren said, went.
<v Adam Schell>达伦一直是每个人都仰望的人。基本上，达伦说什么就是什么。

00:23:49.500 --> 00:23:54.800
<v Young Darren Stein>Action. Camera rolling. Cut.
<v Young Darren Stein>开始。摄像机开动。停。

00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:59.280
<v Ira Glass>And what would it mean to be in one of these films? What would it mean to get a big part in one of these films?
<v Ira Glass>那么成为这些电影的一部分意味着什么？在这些电影里得到一个大角色意味着什么？

00:23:59.280 --> 00:24:09.000
<v Adam Schell>To me, it was the world. To me, it meant everything. It was the most exciting, the most cool thing that we did as kids.
<v Adam Schell>对我来说，那就是全世界。对我来说，那意味着一切。这是我们小时候做的最令人兴奋、最酷的事情。

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:11.410
<v Ira Glass>And would kids vie for parts in the films?
<v Ira Glass>孩子们会争夺电影里的角色吗？

00:24:11.410 --> 00:24:20.230
<v Darren Stein>Totally. I would actually offer the part to one kid, and then decide I didn't want him anymore, offer it to somebody else, and create little dramas behind the scenes.
<v Darren Stein>完全会。我实际上会把角色给一个孩子，然后决定我不想要他了，再给别人，在幕后制造些小冲突。

00:24:20.230 --> 00:25:08.870
<v Adam Schell>As we got older, I think when Darren was in high school and he made a couple of films through his high school drama program, there was more of an auditioning process. The first film he made there was Song From Below . I remember auditioning for that. And I remember Darren giving me the part for that film. And I remember I just felt so cool. And then I remember when he took it away from me, and he gave it to Michael. And I don't remember what his reasoning for it was. In fact, I think he didn't have a specific reasoning. I think he was just like, oh, I'm just going to take it away from you and give it to Michael because I can. And I remember going home and sitting on my bed and crying. It was just utter, crushing defeat.
<v Adam Schell>随着我们长大，我想当达伦上高中，通过他的高中戏剧节目制作了几部电影时，选角过程就更多了。他拍的第一部电影是《底层的歌》。我记得为那部戏试镜。我记得达伦给了我那个角色。然后我记得当他收回它，把它给迈克尔时。我不记得他当时给出的理由是什么。事实上，我觉得他根本没有具体的理由。我觉得他只是觉得，噢，我就是要从你手里拿走给迈克尔，因为我可以。我记得回家坐在床上哭。那简直是彻底的、压倒性的失败。

00:25:08.870 --> 00:25:23.750
<v Ira Glass>You know what it's like, though? It's like, a little kid decides to become a director. And then, not only do they have films to show for it, but their personality becomes like a movie director gone power crazy.
<v Ira Glass>你知道那是什么感觉吗？就像一个小孩子决定成为导演。然后，他们不仅有可以展示的电影，而且他们的个性变得像一个权力疯狂的电影导演。

00:25:23.750 --> 00:25:42.950
<v Adam Schell>Yeah. Yeah, absolutely. And it was a total miniature Hollywood. That's what it was like on our street. And Darren loved that power, and he maintained it the entire time. And he had the power to make you a star, and he had the power to crush you. And the fact that we wanted it so bad, as well--
<v Adam Schell>是啊。是啊，完全是。这就像一个微缩的好莱坞。在我们那条街上就是这样。达伦喜欢那种权力，他全程掌控着。他有能力让你成为明星，也有能力摧毁你。而且我们渴望得到这个，同样——

00:25:42.950 --> 00:25:45.160
<v Ira Glass>--is also so like the real Hollywood.
<v Ira Glass>——也太像真正的好莱坞了。

00:25:45.160 --> 00:25:48.360
<v Adam Schell>Exactly. It's just like the real Hollywood.
<v Adam Schell>没错。这就像真正的好莱坞。

00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:50.340
<v Ira Glass>When you look back on that, do you feel a little embarrassed?
<v Ira Glass>当你回首往事时，你会觉得有点尴尬吗？

00:25:50.340 --> 00:26:00.500
<v Darren Stein>I feel totally embarrassed about that. It was just, I guess, my way of controlling the situation and having fun. And kids are cruel. It was part of that power thing.
<v Darren Stein>我对此完全感到尴尬。我想那只是我控制局面和找乐子的方式。而且孩子们很残忍。那是那种权力游戏的一部分。

00:26:00.500 --> 00:26:14.230
<v Adam Schell>As soon as that camera came out, everybody just crumbled in front of it and did whatever Darren behind the camera ordered us to do. There's some really intense videos that we made as kids.
<v Adam Schell>摄像机一拿出来，每个人就在它面前瘫倒，做任何达伦在摄像机后面命令我们做的事情。我们小时候制作的一些视频真的很激烈。

00:26:14.230 --> 00:26:16.470
<v Ira Glass>What are you thinking about?
<v Ira Glass>你在想什么？

00:26:16.470 --> 00:26:49.900
<v Adam Schell>Well, I mean, I think there's some-- like the Gay as a Whistle film, for example, where Darren puts Allen, who is now openly gay, but at the time, Allen probably knew somewhere in his head, but he wasn't admitting it to the world. And Darren sees this thing in Allen, and maybe it's because they had some sort of underlying communication between the two of them. But he takes that, and he makes a movie about it, and he exploits this thing about Allen that he didn't want anybody in the world to know.
<v Adam Schell>好吧，我的意思是，我想有些——比如《像哨子一样直》那部电影，达伦让艾伦出镜，他现在是公开的同性恋，但在当时，艾伦可能潜意识里知道，但他并没有向世界承认。达伦看到了艾伦身上的这一点，也许是因为他们俩之间有什么潜在的交流。但他拿走这一点，拍了一部关于它的电影，他利用了艾伦不想让世界上任何人知道的事。

00:26:49.900 --> 00:27:10.520
<v Darren Stein>I think I was 12 years old when I made that film. Gay as a Whistle is about a gay guy who has a coin in this little jewelry case. And when he shows you the coin, you turn gay basically. And this is back in the '80s when aerobics was big, and so our moms all wore leotards. And I thought, how cool would it be to put Allen in a leotard?
<v Darren Stein>我想我拍那部电影时才 12 岁。《像哨子一样直》是关于一个同性恋家伙，他有一个小首饰盒里的硬币。当你给你看硬币时，你基本上就会变成同性恋。那还是 80 年代，健美操很流行，所以我们的妈妈们都穿紧身连衣裤。我想，让艾伦穿上紧身连衣裤会有多酷？

00:27:10.520 --> 00:27:13.840
<v Ira Glass>Right. So he's wearing this leotard with lip marks all over it.
<v Ira Glass>对。所以他穿着这件上面印满唇印的紧身连衣裤。

00:27:13.840 --> 00:27:25.630
<v Darren Stein>Exactly. And the film starts out with him sitting in a rocking chair, looking very gay, rocking back and forth. And the camera is right on him. And he turns in to the camera and goes, "Hi, my name is Ramon. And I've got a little secret for you. I'm as gay as a whistle."
<v Darren Stein>没错。电影开头他坐在摇椅上，看起来非常同性恋，摇来摇去。摄像机正对着他。他转向摄像机说，“嗨，我叫拉蒙。我有个小秘密要告诉你。我像哨子一样直。”

00:27:25.630 --> 00:27:37.930
<v Allen>Hi, my name is Ramon. And I've got a little secret for you. I'm as gay as a whistle. I've got this coin here that will make anyone gay when they look at it. Here comes the football team.
